grounding.quote:
preferred shape: a constructor or parser produces a typed carrier;
transforms consume one carrier and return another carrier or a closed
result; projections read those carriers without mutating them.

The required shape: each interface family has
one authoritative source truth; downstream interfaces consume that truth;
crossing an interface boundary does not create a new semantic centre.

Semantic law defines what an evaluation means;
evidence supplies observations; the evaluator applies the declared
relation; decision authority disposes.

A work item closes by the condition it stated, not by a reviewer's approval;
a reviewer result is an input to closure, never the closure. Green labels,
document counts, review counts and historical outcomes are not acceptance.

Bind
any acceptance limits and their owning authority before qualification;
limits and workloads are Product-owned, not universal method constants.

if identity is introduced, identity creation is explicitly owned by
      a declared ingress or effect boundary rather than hidden inside
      semantic helpers;
